  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1205 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nDry weather and above normal temperatures continue during the early \nweek period with highs inching a bit higher Tue-Wed as ridging aloft \nshifts eastward. During the second half of the week, flow aloft over \nour area is progged to turn southwesterly and increase slightly \nduring the second half of the week as the ridge centers over the \nlower MS valley and broad troughing attempts to deepen off the CA \ncoast. Temperatures will therefore come down a bit compared to \nearlier in the week, but will still likely remain just above \nseasonal normals. A modest plume of monsoonal moisture will also \nmake a closer approach to the region thanks to the eastward shift of \nthe ridge, but will remain confined mostly to our west. Isolated to \nscattered afternoon/evening storms over eastern NM may extend into \nfar western portions of the South Plains and SW TX Panhandle each \nday Thu-Sat, but only a weak westerly component to the flow aloft \nwill tend to limit any further eastward expansion of storm activity. \nAs a result, most locations away from the TX/NM state line are \ncurrently expected to remain dry through next weekend.",
